{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Unto Moses and unto Aaron.</b> To Moses He said that he should speak to Aaron." "<b>To say to them.</b> He said that he should speak to Elazar and to Itamar. Or is it not rather to speak to Israel? But when it says ״Speak to the children of Israel,״ behold, a statement addressed to Israel. So how do I establish ״to say to them״? To the sons — to Elazar and to Itamar (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:43.252173171Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}